### Call Android Activity onPause

Source: https://developer.android.com/reference/android/app/Instrumentation

Invokes the onPause method of an Android Activity. This method is available from API level 1 and is used to handle the activity pausing.

```java
public void callActivityOnPause (Activity activity)
```

--------------------------------

### callActivityOnResume

Source: https://developer.android.com/reference/android/app/Instrumentation

Performs the calling of an activity's onResume method.

```APIDOC
## callActivityOnResume

### Description
Perform calling of an activity's `Activity.onResume` method. The default implementation simply calls through to that method.

### Method
`public void callActivityOnResume (Activity activity)`

### Parameters
#### Path Parameters
- None

#### Query Parameters
- None

#### Request Body
- `activity` (Activity) - Required - The activity being resumed.

### Request Example
```json
{
  "activity": "<ActivityObject>"
}
```

### Response
#### Success Response (200)
- None (void method)

#### Response Example
```json
// No response body for void methods
```
```

